        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(sessions): reduce accessor boundary debt",
        "body": "Closes #105785\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nReduces legacy session store and transcript-writer call sites that were still accepted by the session-accessor debt baseline. These exceptions made the canonical storage boundary harder to enforce and obscured that ACP session reads already use an accessor-backed facade.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRoutes suspension writes and SQLite transcript rewrite notifications through `src/config/sessions/session-accessor.ts`, clarifies the ACP manager's accessor-backed dependency name, and regenerates the ratchet baseline. The explicit file-backed transcript notification remains legacy debt because the current accessor cannot preserve that target without an API change.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get six fewer legacy call sites and zero-debt enforcement for the fully migrated files.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/transcript-rewrite.test.ts`: 6 passed\n- `src/agents/session-suspension.test.ts`: 6 passed\n- `src/acp/control-plane/manager.background-task.test.ts` + `manager.test.ts`: 34 passed\n- `test/scripts/check-session-accessor-boundary.test.ts`: 35 passed\n- `node scripts/check-session-accessor-boundary.mjs`: passed\n- Remote `pnpm check:changed`: passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcdkvc734pdwxazsskdbdgx`, [Actions run 29215182675](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29215182675)\n- Structured autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n- Final `git diff --numstat`: 10 files, +31/-32 total; non-test LOC net -3\n",
